ASSISTANT Update the `text` section of the shell script to:
ASSISTANT ```bash
ASSISTANT # Use docopts to parse arguments
ASSISTANT eval "$(docopts -h - : <<'DOCOPTS'
ASSISTANT llm-netogallo: A tool to organize workflows with LLM assistance.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Usage:
ASSISTANT   llm-netogallo [--new-task] [--aider-args=<args>...]
ASSISTANT   llm-netogallo (-h | --help)
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Options:
ASSISTANT   --new-task       Start a new task.
ASSISTANT   --aider-args=<args>  Arguments to pass to aider.
ASSISTANT   -h, --help       Show this help.
ASSISTANT DOCOPTS
ASSISTANT )"
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT # Check if --new-task is set
ASSISTANT if ${is-enabled} [[ "$CURRENT_BRANCH" != "${task-branch-prefix}"* ]] && { [[ -z "$ARG_new_task" ]] || [[ "$ARG_new_task" != "true" ]]; }; then
ASSISTANT   aider "${ARG_aider_args[@]}"
ASSISTANT   exit 0
ASSISTANT fi
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT # Rest of the script remains the same, but use --new-task logic
ASSISTANT if [[ "$ARG_new_task" == "true" ]]; then
ASSISTANT   read -rp "Starting a new task. What is the task name? " task_name
ASSISTANT   echo "$task_name" > "$LLM_CURRENT_TASK_FILE"
ASSISTANT fi
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT # Forward aider args at the end
ASSISTANT aider \
ASSISTANT   --read "$TASK_INPUT_FILE" \
ASSISTANT   --read "$LLM_ACTIVE_TASK_FILE" \
ASSISTANT   --llm-history-file "$LLM_SESSION_CONTEXT_DIR/$LLM_TASK/llm.history" \
ASSISTANT   --chat-history-file "$LLM_SESSION_CONTEXT_DIR/$LLM_TASK/session.md" "${ARG_aider_args[@]}"
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ### Notes:
ASSISTANT - The `docopts` parsing is added at the start of the script.
ASSISTANT - `--new-task` is optional and only triggers new task logic when provided.
ASSISTANT - All other arguments are forwarded to `aider` via `${ARG_aider_args[@]}`.
