ASSISTANT    if [ "$help" = "true" ]; then
ASSISTANT        docopts -h - : <<'DOCOPTS'  # Re-print help and exit
ASSISTANT        ...
ASSISTANT        exit 0
ASSISTANT    fi
ASSISTANT    ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ### Why This Works:
ASSISTANT - `docopts` now receives the script’s arguments (`--help`, `--new-task`, etc.) and parses them correctly.
ASSISTANT - The `eval` applies the parsed variables to the shell environment, so you can check `$help` or `$new_task`.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ### For Your Script:
ASSISTANT Update the `docopts` line to include `"$@"`, and ensure you check the parsed flags afterward. This will make `--help` and other flags work as expected.
